-- title:
--   Label unit isolating one branch through a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ and $\ell$ are primes, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ satisfies $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Level and function field.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is required (`hH₁`) to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((T))$ is required (`hK`) to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   **Base ring and chart algebra.** $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$; $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and its Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= T^{-1}\cdot jNum_{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hj`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ regarded in $C$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The integral model and the point above $y$.** $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two morphisms from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras. The point $z \in X$, the element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ obtained (`hϖz`) as the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ along `toBase`, and the hypothesis `hz` that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk are given; $y'$ is a point of `XFin A ↥K j` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`), with the same supersingularity requirement `hss'` at $y'$ and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart witness.** $W_1$ is a discrete valuation domain, complete for the $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$-adic topology, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`); $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`, the comparison being with [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and $e_1$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$.
--
--   **The rider `hW₁`.** With `STK` the stalk at $z$, `CMP` its adic completion, `toC : STK → CMP` the canonical map, `mkS : W₁[[X₀,X₁]] → S` the quotient map, and `germY : C → STK` the canonical homomorphism (germ at $z$ on the image of `ιFin`, composed with the inverses of the relevant ring isomorphisms), `hW₁` is a seven-fold conjunction, whose clauses are:
--   (i) for every $a \in A$, $e_1$ applied to the image in `CMP` of the germ at $z$ of the section coming from $a$ is the class of the constant $\sigma_1(a)$;
--   (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the predicate asserting that for all weights $k$ and all modular forms $f,g$ of level `GammaH (q^2*M') H₁` with integral $q$-expansions and $g$'s expansion non-zero, and all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of the ratio of those expansions, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under any $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i /q}$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where `conjElemN q δ` is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q\\ q\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$;
--   (iii) for every such $\gamma$ which moreover satisfies $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, every such $\tau$ and every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ preserves $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ satisfies $\tau a - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$;
--   (iv) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as in (ii), every proof that $\tau$ preserves $C$, and on the assumption that $\tau a - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines the action of $\tau$ on $C$ with the identification $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$; $\theta$ fixes the class of every constant; $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_{j}) - \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_i M_{ij}X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$; $M_{ij} - c\,\gamma_{ij} \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$;
--   (v) for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ omits at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, contains the class of the constant $\sigma_1\varpi$, and contains an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct;
--   (vi) for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma_1\varpi$ and containing $X_0 + h$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a \in C$: the image $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L((T))$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$;
--   (vii) the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), obtained from the $j$-expansion by multiplying all exponents by $q$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, first, for all $a,b \in W_1$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W_1$, and second, $e_1$ carries the image in `CMP` of the germ of that element minus $a_0$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The Ogg profile of $g$.** Finally $g \in C$ is non-zero in $K$ (`hg0`), divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$ in the sense that $g z = \varpi^k$ in $C$ for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $z \in C$ (`hgϖ`), is fixed by every $\tau$ attached as in (ii) to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hginv`), and satisfies the translate profile (`hgprof`): for every $\delta \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ attached to $\delta^{-1}$, all Laurent coefficients of $\tau g$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ if and only if $q \nmid \delta_{10}$.
--
--   **Data of the conclusion.** $\mathfrak{p}$ is a prime ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, contained in $y$ and distinct from $y$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist $u \in C$ and a proof that $u$ is non-zero as an element of $K$, such that: (1) $u$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$, i.e. $u z = \varpi^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $z \in C$; (2) $\tau u = u$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`; (3) $u \notin \mathfrak{p}$; and (4) $u \in \mathfrak{p}'$ for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}'$ of $C$ which contains the image of $\varpi$, is contained in $y$, and is distinct from both $y$ and $\mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   This is the step which converts the translate profile of a function $g$ under the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action (Ogg's criterion, recording for which $\delta$ the translate $\tau g$ has integral coefficients in $\mathfrak m_A$) into a unit attached to a single label: an element of the $j$-finite chart algebra dividing a power of the uniformiser, invariant under the $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-attached automorphisms, and lying in every branch through the supersingular point $y$ except the chosen one $\mathfrak p$. It is formulated in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame, with the guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, so that it applies for all primes $q$; it is used in the construction of label units on the components of the special fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
